            <title>0.4.6</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:08:42 -0400</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/templetongroup/Kiki/releases/tag/v0.4.6</link>
            <sparkle:version>14</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# Kiki 0.4.6

This release fixes mouse interaction across Kiki’s custom navigation controls.

## What’s fixed

- Sidebar buttons now respond to ordinary mouse clicks throughout Settings.
- Personalization Studio navigation receives the same shared correction.
- Custom action and information buttons no longer allow their clicks to be interpreted as window dragging.
- Sidebar controls respond on the first click even when their window was previously inactive.

The root cause was a hit-test coordinate mismatch: parent-space mouse positions were being compared with local button bounds. Keyboard and accessibility activation worked, but physical clicks on later sidebar rows were rejected.

Transcription speed, quality, and Kiki’s fully local privacy model remain unchanged.
]]></description>
